=== Climate ===
Shimabara Prefecture has a tropical monsoon climate with highland volcanic modification (Köppen ''Am''), characterised by warm temperatures, heavy rainfall, and the moderating influence of the volcanic terrain. The highland interior, at 500–1,600 m elevation, experiences significantly cooler temperatures than the surrounding lowlands, with frequent morning fog, cool nights, and lower humidity—conditions that are ideal for both wasabi cultivation and sake brewing.

The volcanic topography creates distinctive microclimates. The windward slopes of the Shimabara Volcanic Group receive orographic rainfall that can exceed 4,000 mm annually, while the leeward valleys sit in a partial rain shadow that provides the drier conditions preferred by wasabi. The volcanic springs maintain a constant flow of cool, mineral-rich water regardless of seasonal rainfall, ensuring stable growing conditions for the terraced wasabi fields.

